---
/* OFF THE ICE — 04/10/2026, Session 28 (docs/roadmap.md). The conditioning
   collection, which has had a schema and no entries since August. Each entry names a
   capacity and the elements that need it; the programme is left to a coach or a
   physiotherapist, which is the rule written into content.config.ts and the reason
   this is not a workout page. General fitness is better covered elsewhere. */
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { url } from '../../lib/url.js';
/* The order a skater needs them in: balance and the knee from the first lessons, then
   what the jumps and spins ask for, then what a whole programme asks for. */
const ORDER = ['balance-on-one-leg', 'a-deep-soft-knee', 'hips-and-turnout', 'core-and-carriage',
  'holding-the-landing', 'jumping-and-turning-off-the-floor', 'spotting-and-rotation', 'spin-positions', 'stamina'];
const entries = (await getCollection('conditioning')).sort((a, b) => ORDER.indexOf(a.id) - ORDER.indexOf(b.id));
const unplaced = entries.filter(e => !ORDER.includes(e.id));
if (unplaced.length) throw new Error(`off-ice: ${unplaced.map(e => e.id).join(', ')} has no place in ORDER`);
---
<Base title="Off the ice" subtitle="What the body needs for the elements, and which elements need it.">
  <h1>Off the ice</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    Each page here names something the body has to be able to do, says which elements ask
    for it, and leaves the programme to a coach or a physiotherapist.
  </p>
  <p>
    That is deliberate. A website cannot see how you move, and a squat or a stretch is
    better taught by someone who can. What the guide can do is connect the work to the ice:
    why a skater needs a held single-leg bend, and which jumps fall apart without one. Every
    element named below links back here from its own page.
  </p>
  <p>
    Warm up before anything off the ice, and before jumping above all. Jump on a forgiving
    surface, land on a bent knee, and stop if something hurts. A skater with an injury or a
    health condition should ask a doctor or physiotherapist first.
  </p>

  <h2>What the elements ask for</h2>
  <ul class="plain">
    {entries.map(e => (
      <li>
        <a href={url(`off-ice/${e.id}/`)}>{e.data.name}</a>
        <span>{e.data.summary} {e.data.prepares.length} element{e.data.prepares.length === 1 ? '' : 's'} named.</span>
      </li>
    ))}
  </ul>

</Base>
